 # Markdown heading catalog
 
-Existing action line_count is exposed through api.dispatch and python cli.py, accepting one JSON object on stdin and writing one JSON result.
+Actions are dispatched through `api.dispatch(payload)` and `python cli.py`, which accepts one JSON object on stdin and writes one JSON result to stdout.
+
+Existing action `line_count` returns the number of `splitlines()` lines in `payload.markdown`.
+
+New action `headings` requires `markdown` to be a string of at most 10000 code points; a longer string raises `ValueError` (CLI exit 2, nonempty stderr, no traceback). It returns a list of objects `{level, text, line, anchor}` for ATX headings found outside fenced code blocks. Fence lines are any line whose stripped text starts with three backticks; each toggles fenced mode and is excluded, as are all lines inside fences. Outside fences, a heading is a line starting at column zero with 1..6 `#` followed by exactly one ASCII space; the text is the remainder stripped at both ends (trailing `#` are ordinary text). Anchors: lowercase, keep only ASCII a-z/0-9 and spaces/hyphens, collapse each run of spaces/hyphens to one hyphen, trim hyphens; an empty base becomes `section`. Duplicates get `-2`, `-3`, ... suffixes in document order.
+
+Example invocation:
+
+```bash
+echo '{"action":"headings","markdown":"# Title\n## Title"}' | python cli.py
+# -> [{"level": 1, "text": "Title", "line": 1, "anchor": "title"}, {"level": 2, "text": "Title", "line": 2, "anchor": "title-2"}]
+```
+
+Boundary semantics: exactly 10000 code points is accepted; 10001 is rejected with `ValueError`. Unknown actions raise `ValueError` ("unknown action: ..."), and the CLI exits 2 with the message on stderr and no traceback. Input objects are never mutated.
